{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115264","id":3199329964,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6-seas","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115264","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115264.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115264.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115264","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115264/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115264/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115264/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/9fde44f801f9e4a0ab02f867ae6f0cbbf2a676bd","number":115264,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add editor setting to enable or disable selecting tilemaplayer via click","user":{"login":"taedixon","id":6359597,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTk1OTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6359597?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon","html_url":"https://github.com/taedixon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Summary of Changes\r\nAdd an editor setting to allow the user to configure whether clicking a tile in the scene should select the associated TileMapLayer in the SceneTree.\r\n\r\n# Motivation\r\nMakes it possible to opt-out of the behaviour introduced in #92016.\r\n \r\nWith a TileMapLayer selected, the left mouse button's behaviour is dictated by the active tool in the Tile editor e.g. Paint Tool, Rect Tool, Bucket Tool. While this is expected and indeed necessary for the Tile editor to work, this creates a \"one-way street\" when clicking on an element in the scene may put you into this context as it is no longer possible to click on any other element in the scene to exit it. The ~~only~~ way to return to Select mode is to manually click any non-TileMapLayer node in the Scene Tree *(or press the Escape key!)*. \r\n\r\nThis issue is compounded by the nature of TileMapLayers typically taking up the majority of the clickable surface in scenes where they are used, resulting in slight misclicks of sprites or other scene elements necessitating another click on the SceneTree to fix Select behaviour, and then re-finding and clicking the element one was originally intending to select. \r\n\r\nWhile it is possible to \"work around\" this behaviour by locking and un-locking TileMapLayer nodes as you edit them, I find this a bit tedious when iterating and it's easy to forget to lock or unlock a node every time you're done using it.\r\n\r\nI have personally found this to be a cause of frustration and lost productivity, and there may be others that feel the same. Allowing a simple checkbox to return the behaviour present in 4.2 and earlier for those that prefer it seems to me a good solution for all parties. \r\n\r\n# Testing\r\n1. Create or open a scene containing TileMapLayer node(s)\r\n2. Locate the editor setting `Editors -> Tiles Editor -> Click to Select Tilemap` (requires Advanced Settings checkbox)\r\n3. With the setting checked, observe that clicking on a tile in Select mode selects a TileMapLayer in the scene tree.\r\n4. With the setting unchecked, observe that clicking on a tile in Select mode does not select anything (but clicking on other nodes still selects them as usual).","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","description":"","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-01-22T13:11:43Z","updated_at":"2026-02-07T12:36:44Z","closed_at":"2026-01-22T14:12:46Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"3980b3afd8a487e5023e365b586665258fcfb6f9","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"taedixon:tilemap-select-option","ref":"tilemap-select-option","repo":{"id":764844807,"node_id":"R_kgDOLZabBw","name":"godot","full_name":"taedixon/godot","owner":{"login":"taedixon","id":6359597,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzNTk1OTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6359597?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon","html_url":"https://github.com/taedixon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/taedixon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.